---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const description = 'Rehearse one real AI workflow with your team. Explore the One-Day AI Work Lab, 30-Day AI Work Rehearsal and ongoing Rehearsal Practice.';
---
<Base title="The Rehearsal Room | AI Work Labs" description={description} path="/rehearsal-room/">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Rehearsal Room</p>
    <h1>Try the work before the stakes are real.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Bring one consequential workflow and the people who own it. Rehearse what happens when AI joins the work, including the moments when it gets something wrong.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/?topic=rehearsal-day">Talk about your workflow</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#formats">Find the right format</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap page-body">
    <h2>One real piece of work</h2>
    <p>A customer handoff. A first draft that someone must verify. A decision that needs a person to remain in control. Start with work your team recognizes, then make the roles, data, permissions and boundaries visible.</p>
    <p>For example, a team might rehearse an AI-assisted customer reply. First, the ordinary request. Then an ambiguous request, missing information or a confident mistake. Who notices? Who can interrupt? What happens next? This is an example of a rehearsal scene, not a client result.</p>
    <div class="section-rule" id="formats">
      <h2>Choose the depth of rehearsal</h2>
      <ul class="cards">
        <li class="card" id="build"><p class="eyebrow">Start with one workflow</p><h3>One-Day AI Work Lab</h3><p>A cross-functional team runs a normal scene and a pressure scene. Together, we define the work, cast people and tools, rehearse the handoffs and interpret what happened.</p><p><strong>Leave with:</strong> a workflow map, observed risks, evidence from the scenes and a Pilot / Revise / Stop decision.</p><a href="/contact/?topic=rehearsal-day">Ask about the one-day lab →</a></li>
        <li class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Build through repetition</p><h3>30-Day AI Work Rehearsal</h3><p>Put the workflow through role-specific repetitions. Practice verification, interruption and recovery. Test whether the people doing the work can use it, including accessibility needs and exceptions.</p><p><strong>Leave with:</strong> evidence of what holds up, what needs to change and an operating playbook the team can use.</p><a href="/contact/?topic=rehearsal-30">Ask about the 30-day rehearsal →</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="section-rule" id="practice"><span id="own"></span><h2>Rehearsal Practice</h2><p>Work changes. People join. Tools behave differently. Keep the practice alive through recurring scenes, coaching and failure drills. Use what the team observes to decide what to keep, revise or stop.</p><p><a href="/contact/?topic=practice">Talk about an ongoing practice →</a></p></div>
    <div class="section-rule"><h2>How we work</h2><p>TheaterThink® brings rehearsal-room craft to consequential work: <strong>Direct → Cast → Rehearse → Interpret.</strong> Define what matters, assemble the people and tools, try the work, then read the evidence before deciding what comes next.</p><p><a href="/how-we-work/">See the method →</a> · <a href="/executive-advisory/">Explore Transformation Advisory →</a></p></div>
    <div class="section-rule"><h2>Before we begin</h2>
      <h3>Do we need AI or theater experience?</h3><p>No. Bring knowledge of the work and the people affected by it. The rehearsal starts there.</p>
      <h3>Which workflow should we choose?</h3><p>Choose a bounded piece of work with recognizable inputs, handoffs and consequences. The first conversation helps identify a useful starting point.</p>
      <h3>What about sensitive data and permissions?</h3><p>Agree on data, tools, access and human decision rights before the rehearsal. Use approved or representative material. Do not include confidential information in the inquiry form.</p>
      <h3>Can our team participate remotely?</h3><p>Tell us where the team works and any access needs. We will shape the format around the people and the workflow.</p>
      <h3>What happens after I get in touch?</h3><p>We review the situation with you, identify the people who need to be involved and decide whether a lab, a longer rehearsal or advisory work fits. Scope comes before a proposal.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/?topic=rehearsal-day">Bring us the work you are stuck on</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
